{"n": 211, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "211.webp", "text": "12-112 /6\n\nFAULT 73\n\n900 fault memory: 73 road speed signal\n\nExplanation: This fault is stored by OME when following conditions are fulfilled\nsimultaneously.\n\nEngine speed » 4500 rpm\n\nLoad signal 5.0 ms\n\nRoad speed signal 3 to 5 km/h (2 to 3 mph)\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT 76\n\n900 faull memory: 76 Idie speed CO potentiometer\n\nExplanation: Valld only for cars without catalytic converter. This taull Is stored\nwhen shorts or breaks occur on potentiometer or Its leads. Replacement value\nof 2.77 V Is used.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen, Test values — see component testing.\nFAULT 77\n\n900 fault memory: 77 intake air temperature sensor\n\nExplanation: This fault is stored when shorts or breaks occur on temperature\nsensor or ts leads. Recognition of a break requires 3 minutes time after starl-\nIng and idle speed for at least 30 seconds. Replacement value of 50° C (122° F)\nis used after recognition of fault,\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen. Test values - see component testing.\nFAULT 78\n\n900 fault memory: 78 engine temperature sensor\n\nExplanation: This fault Is stored when shorts or breaks occur on temperature.\nsensor or Its leads.\n\nIntake alr temperature Is used as a replacement value in case of fault, but only\nfor the first 3 minutes after starting when air temperature Is < 20° C (60° F). A re-\nplacement value of 80° C (176° F) Is ready for use In other conditions.\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen. Test values — see component testing.\nFAULT 85\n\n900 fault memory: 85 alr conditioner compressor\n\nExplanation: This fault Is stored when control unit receives “compressor In\noperation” (batlery voltage on pin 85) and “A/C switch not operated” (0 V on\npin 86) signals simultaneously. In this case either pin 86 has a break or there Is\n@ short between baltery vollage and pin 85.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT 100\n900 fault memory: 100 final stage\n\nExplanation: This fault is stored when a loose contact occurs on a final stage\noutput. If another final stage fault (Fault Codes 1, 3, 18, 29, 32, 36 or 37) occurs\nadditionally, it can be assumed that fault 100 ts Identical with one of these\nfaults.\n\nFAULT 200\n3900 fault memory: 200 DME control unit\n\nExplanation: This fault Is stored when the internal self-test finds a fault in the\nmemory modules (manipulated data),\n\nPossible causes: programming fault or disturbed program run-off in DME con-\ntral unit. This fault will also be stored when programming of the control unit\nhad been manipulated. In this case the locks on the contro! unit housing will be\ndamaged.\n\nCorrection: Test drive car afier cancelling the fault memory. DME control unit\nmust be replaced If the fault occurs again.\n\nFAULT 207\n900 fault memory: 201 oxygen sensor control\n\nExplanation: This fault is stored in case of excessive deviation in the fuel/air\nmixture (excessively rich or lean mixture for longer than 12 seconds). it re-\nquires an oxygen sensor ready for operation.\n\nPossible Causes of Fault:\n\n- Wrong fuel pressure\n\nFaulty or carbonized fuel injectors\n\nFaulty engine temperature sensor\n\nWrong alr In intake\n\nFaulty tank venting system\n\nOlrty spark plug\n\nLeak In exhaust system In front of oxygen sensor\nFaulty alr flow sensor\n\nImpaired combustion (ignition or compression nol okay)\n\nmt\n\nrrid\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen. Test values — see component testing\nand technical data microfiche.", "words": [["12-112", 0.4459, 0.0298, 0.5217, 0.0522], ["/6", 0.5288, 0.0311, 0.549, 0.0536], ["FAULT", 0.0217, 0.0813, 0.0592, 0.0933], ["73", 0.0632, 0.0827, 0.0753, 0.0933], ["900", 0.0207, 0.1151, 0.0399, 0.1257], ["fault", 0.045, 0.1151, 0.0683, 0.127], ["memory:", 0.0723, 0.1177, 0.1173, 0.1296], ["73", 0.1223, 0.1151, 0.1335, 0.127], ["road", 0.1375, 0.1164, 0.1608, 0.127], ["speed", 0.1648, 0.1164, 0.1962, 